 "title": "Pick a spot to hide from lightning: under a tree, in a lake, lying flat, or in a car",
 "format": "pick-a-scenario",
 "root": "/home/claude/b3d/bolt",
 "lines": [
  "Three of these spots are lightning traps.",
  "Pick one: where do you hide when lightning starts?",
  "Under a tree, in a lake, flat on the ground, or in a car.",
  "Pick one, two, three or four, and comment. Think fast.",
  "Number one, the tree. It keeps you dry, and that's the trap.",
  "Sheltering under trees is the second leading cause of lightning casualties.",
  "A strike can jump from the trunk into you. That's called a side flash.",
  "Number two, the lake. A strike's current spreads out through the water, and through you.",
  "Number three, lying flat. Staying low sounds smart.",
  "But the biggest killer isn't a direct hit. It's current racing through the ground.",
  "Lie flat, and you give that current more of your body.",
  "Number four, the car, with a hard metal roof and the windows up.",
  "And it's not the rubber tires. They give zero protection.",
  "The metal shell carries the strike around you and into the ground.",
  "That bolt heats the air to fifty thousand degrees Fahrenheit, five times hotter than the Sun's surface.",
  "So the winner is number four. Just never a convertible.",
  "Park ranger Roy Sullivan was struck seven times, and survived them all.",
  "About nine in ten people who get struck survive. But remember:"
 ],
